<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29996" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mūnĭfex</span></b> ,
			ĭcis, com.
		munia-facio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>one who performs service</i> or <i>is
				on duty</i> (postAug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, of soldiers: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">munifices, milites, qui munera facere coguntur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Veg. Mil. 2, 7</span></i>
			; cf. Paul. ex Fest. s. v. BENEFICIARII, p. 33
			Müll.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, of things: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">munifex mamma,</span>”
				i. e. <i>suckling</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 40, 95, § 234</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
